Pages = {142-148},
Month = {MAY},
Abstract = {Human-induced pressures are known to be one of the main causes of
   biodiversity loss. In order to readily assess policy impacts on
   biodiversity, a cost-effective evaluation tool is developed, using
   species sensitivity scores. We demonstrate the potential effects of a
   selected policy option, being woody bioenergy crop production, on a wide
   range of species groups in Europe. Large-scale expansions of woody
   biofuel plantations would have a net negative effect on the species set
   covered in our study, with little variation among biogeographical
   regions, but with considerable differences among species groups. The
   evaluation tool enables policy makers to assess the potential impact of
   decisions on future biodiversity. (C) 2009 Elsevier GmbH. All rights
   reserved.},
